(6851896, 1030045, 80908, '<td valign="top">Hi Posthmous, we meet again in the Critique Zone!<br/> <br/>Hmmm. Normally I am a fan, but this one doesn''t grab me. I like the dog although I am a little mystified by the barcode through the nose. I am just not sure what the blur adds to this, it doesn''t seem to me to need a sense of movement or dynamism. The flat, desert beige colours tell me that everything there should be still, beaten down by the heat. Perhaps I am wrong and it is heat haze not motion blur?<br/> <br/>I think what really leaves me cold is just the overall balance of the composition. The tilted angle, the extra space at the top. I guess I just don''t get it! Having seen plenty of your work, I''m sure you had something in mind here but this time, I''m not sure what it is.<br/> <br/>I''m going to head back to predictability and over-sharpening now!<br/> <br/>Happy hunting,<br/> <br/>Frank.</td>', 'Hi Posthmous, we meet again in the Critique Zone! Hmmm. Normally I am a fan, but this one doesn''t grab me. I like the dog although I am a little mystified by the barcode through the nose. I am just not sure what the blur adds to this, it doesn''t seem to me to need a sense of movement or dynamism. The flat, desert beige colours tell me that everything there should be still, beaten down by the heat. Perhaps I am wrong and it is heat haze not motion blur? I think what really leaves me cold is just the overall balance of the composition. The tilted angle, the extra space at the top. I guess I just don''t get it! Having seen plenty of your work, I''m sure you had something in mind here but this time, I''m not sure what it is. I''m going to head back to predictability and over-sharpening now! Happy hunting, Frank.', '2012-08-29 17:10:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6851904, 1029775, 80908, '<td valign="top">HI Quincy, Welcome to the Critique Zone!<br/> <br/>This is a cracking shot! Instantly eye catching but with enough depth to keep me interested for a while. Shame DPC voters only have 30 seconds to vote...<br/> <br/>Technically, this looks fairly immaculate. I definitely think that it needs the full DOF that you have achieved to give the background detail. Nice and sharp, etc.<br/> <br/>The real strength though is in the artistry. Really nice perspective, perfect use of the rule of thirds and an outstanding black and white conversion. This would only have worked so well from this side too - with the traffic driving away. Very emotive.<br/> <br/>Why didn''t it score? I guess the voters didn''t see the fit to the challenge. That''s all I can guess at. It may feel like a kick in the nuts but I wouldn''t care if I were you - this is a keeper.<br/> <br/>Happy hunting,<br/> <br/>Frank.</td>', 'HI Quincy, Welcome to the Critique Zone! This is a cracking shot! Instantly eye catching but with enough depth to keep me interested for a while. Shame DPC voters only have 30 seconds to vote... Technically, this looks fairly immaculate. I definitely think that it needs the full DOF that you have achieved to give the background detail. Nice and sharp, etc. The real strength though is in the artistry. Really nice perspective, perfect use of the rule of thirds and an outstanding black and white conversion. This would only have worked so well from this side too - with the traffic driving away. Very emotive. Why didn''t it score? I guess the voters didn''t see the fit to the challenge. That''s all I can guess at. It may feel like a kick in the nuts but I wouldn''t care if I were you - this is a keeper. Happy hunting, Frank.', '2012-08-29 17:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6851983, 1029775, 141542, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by FrankRobinson:</b></div><hr/><i> HI Quincy, Welcome to the Critique Zone!<br/> <br/>This is a cracking shot! Instantly eye catching but with enough depth to keep me interested for a while. Shame DPC voters only have 30 seconds to vote...<br/> <br/>Technically, this looks fairly immaculate. I definitely think that it needs the full DOF that you have achieved to give the background detail. Nice and sharp, etc.<br/> <br/>The real strength though is in the artistry. Really nice perspective, perfect use of the rule of thirds and an outstanding black and white conversion. This would only have worked so well from this side too - with the traffic driving away. Very emotive.<br/> <br/>Why didn''t it score? I guess the voters didn''t see the fit to the challenge. That''s all I can guess at. It may feel like a kick in the nuts but I wouldn''t care if I were you - this is a keeper.<br/> <br/>Happy hunting,<br/> <br/>Frank. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Frank. I appreciate the critique, one of the few I''ve had that had no negative points and that''s why I value honest critique. Thanks also for taking the time out of your day to do it.</td>', 'Originally posted by FrankRobinson: HI Quincy, Welcome to the Critique Zone! This is a cracking shot! Instantly eye catching but with enough depth to keep me interested for a while. Shame DPC voters only have 30 seconds to vote... Technically, this looks fairly immaculate. I definitely think that it needs the full DOF that you have achieved to give the background detail. Nice and sharp, etc. The real strength though is in the artistry. Really nice perspective, perfect use of the rule of thirds and an outstanding black and white conversion. This would only have worked so well from this side too - with the traffic driving away. Very emotive. Why didn''t it score? I guess the voters didn''t see the fit to the challenge. That''s all I can guess at. It may feel like a kick in the nuts but I wouldn''t care if I were you - this is a keeper. Happy hunting, Frank.   Thanks Frank. I appreciate the critique, one of the few I''ve had that had no negative points and that''s why I value honest critique. Thanks also for taking the time out of your day to do it.', '2012-08-29 19:49:19.000000', NULL, 0),
